 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate Technology Consultant position at Reply in London. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have sat between business stakeholders and technical work: understanding what people need, translating it into something that can be built and tested, and explaining the result. I am particularly interested in this role because that bridge is the core of it.",

 r"What attracts me most to Reply is its focus on emerging technologies such as AI and cloud, its network of specialised companies working across many sectors, and the emphasis on learning through certifications, hackathons and lab camps. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and operations data in SQL and Python and build KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. I also built an AI agent using Claude Code that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, and it is now used by my own team and by adjacent teams. Building it meant understanding the existing process, deciding which steps the agent should own and which still needed a person, and supporting colleagues as they adopted it.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a medical AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I gathered requirements from the client's clinical experts and translated them into a 246-question benchmark and six-dimension rubric, which the client adopted as its acceptance standard. I then built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses, and presented the findings and priorities to clinical and business stakeholders.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I analysed more than 80 healthcare professional interviews, built market-sizing and forecasting models, and turned findings into dashboards and recommendations for client stakeholders. My MSc dissertation used 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as an interactive Streamlit application, so I am used to turning technical work into something non-specialists can use.",

